# Milestone: M6
# Covers: Phase 6 (T38) — nested-class shadow scoping (S-class-name-scope).
#
# When a class shadows a binding by the same name, its proto reference
# must resolve to the OUTER binding.  Per spec, the parser does not bind
# the class name before parsing the proto list and body; the emit binds
# the class name as a local AFTER body emit completes.  So inside
#
#   class a { var foo = 40 }; class a : public a { var bar = 2 }
#
# the second `: public a` resolves to the FIRST class `a` (the one that
# defined foo).  The inner `a` then inherits foo from the outer and adds
# bar locally.

# b inherits foo (via outer a) and bar (via inner a).
class a { var foo = 40 }; class a : public a { var bar = 2 }; var b = a.new(); b.foo + b.bar
[00000000] 42
